               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="11XX/12XX">s. xii/xiii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_143">Cirencester, Gloucestershire.
                        Augustinian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>"Liber magistri
                        Aluredi" in red capitals on the flyleaf, as in Jesus Coll. 26 and All Souls
                        Coll. 82.</p><p>A note of contents in Sir John Prise's hand occurs in this
                        MS. and in fourteen other MSS. at Hereford. These fourteen are all
                        Cirencester books. The probablity that O.ii.4 is also from Cirencester is
                        confirmed by the inscription in the All Souls MS. (q. v.). Prise did not
                        write a note of contents in the MSS. which he obtained from Bury,
                        Tewkesbury, Gloucester, Winchcombe, Pershore, Bristol, and St Guthlac's,
                        Hereford.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir John Prise. </provenance>
               </history>
